WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.863
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.163 --> 00:00:08.549
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.849 --> 00:00:13.800
Unit nine: Personality. In this unit, you will describe people's personalities.

4
00:00:14.817 --> 00:00:15.528
Friendly.

5
00:00:16.228 --> 00:00:18.552
Friendly means kind and nice to other people.

6
00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.585
Our neighbours are very friendly.

7
00:00:21.285 --> 00:00:24.169
Your turn. Say: Friendly.

8
00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:27.743
Friendly.

9
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.798
Shy.

10
00:00:30.498 --> 00:00:32.961
Shy means nervous about talking to new people.

11
00:00:33.261 --> 00:00:34.762
She is shy at first.

12
00:00:35.462 --> 00:00:37.986
Your turn. Say: Shy.

13
00:00:40.686 --> 00:00:41.502
Shy.

14
00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:43.378
Honest.

15
00:00:44.078 --> 00:00:46.508
Honest means always telling the truth.

16
00:00:46.808 --> 00:00:48.621
An honest person never lies.

17
00:00:49.321 --> 00:00:52.125
Your turn. Say: Honest.

18
00:00:54.825 --> 00:00:55.733
Honest.

19
00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:57.590
Lazy.

20
00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.150
Lazy means not wanting to work.

21
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.148
My cat is very lazy.

22
00:01:02.848 --> 00:01:05.454
Your turn. Say: Lazy.

23
00:01:08.154 --> 00:01:09.004
Lazy.

24
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:11.018
Hard-working.

25
00:01:11.718 --> 00:01:14.518
Hard-working means working with a lot of effort.

26
00:01:14.818 --> 00:01:16.319
Farmers are hard-working.

27
00:01:17.019 --> 00:01:19.868
Your turn. Say: Hard-working.

28
00:01:22.568 --> 00:01:23.732
Hard-working.

29
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.567
Patient.

30
00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.278
Patient means able to wait calmly.

31
00:01:28.578 --> 00:01:30.218
A good teacher is patient.

32
00:01:30.918 --> 00:01:33.187
Your turn. Say: Patient.

33
00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:36.818
Patient.

34
00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:38.678
Generous.

35
00:01:39.378 --> 00:01:41.517
Generous means happy to give and share.

36
00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:43.712
My grandma is very generous.

37
00:01:44.412 --> 00:01:47.355
Your turn. Say: Generous.

38
00:01:50.055 --> 00:01:51.195
Generous.

39
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:53.289
Personality.

40
00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:56.813
Personality means the kind of person you are inside.

41
00:01:57.113 --> 00:01:58.950
She has a kind personality.

42
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.256
Your turn. Say: Personality.

43
00:02:04.956 --> 00:02:06.073
Personality.

44
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:09.164
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:09.464 --> 00:02:11.371
Sreypich, what's your brother like?

46
00:02:12.683 --> 00:02:14.648
He's really friendly and generous.

47
00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.381
Is he hard-working?

48
00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:21.684
Not always. He's a bit lazy at weekends!

49
00:02:22.983 --> 00:02:24.275
And what about you?

50
00:02:25.583 --> 00:02:27.850
I'm quite shy, but I'm really patient.

51
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.355
Grammar focus: Adjectives plus really and quite and a bit.

52
00:02:33.655 --> 00:02:36.145
She is really patient. He is a bit lazy.

53
00:02:36.445 --> 00:02:40.999
Use 'a bit' mostly with negative adjectives: a bit lazy, a bit shy.

54
00:02:41.983 --> 00:02:44.589
Now read and listen. Everyone Is Different.

55
00:02:44.889 --> 00:02:47.121
People have different personalities.

56
00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:51.554
My brother is friendly and generous, but he can be a bit lazy.

57
00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.082
My sister is shy and really patient.

58
00:02:56.383 --> 00:02:59.579
My best friend is quite funny and always honest.

59
00:03:00.883 --> 00:03:03.603
I try to be honest and hard-working every day.

60
00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:07.441
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:07.741 --> 00:03:09.729
He is blank lazy on Sundays.

62
00:03:10.029 --> 00:03:13.079
A, a bit. B, a lot. C, much.

63
00:03:17.083 --> 00:03:19.002
The answer is A: a bit.

64
00:03:20.517 --> 00:03:22.725
Always telling the truth means blank.

65
00:03:23.025 --> 00:03:26.110
A, honest. B, shy. C, lazy.

66
00:03:30.117 --> 00:03:31.710
The answer is A: honest.

67
00:03:33.217 --> 00:03:35.437
Able to wait calmly means blank.

68
00:03:35.737 --> 00:03:39.146
A, patient. B, generous. C, friendly.

69
00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.150
The answer is A: patient.

70
00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:50.661
Now it's your turn to speak. What three words describe your personality?

71
00:03:55.961 --> 00:03:59.562
I am quite friendly, really hard-working and a bit shy with new people.

72
00:03:59.862 --> 00:04:01.641
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:07.462
Great work today! You learned eight new words and adjectives plus really and quite and a bit.

74
00:04:07.762 --> 00:04:12.249
Today's value is self-awareness. Know your strengths and keep growing.

75
00:04:12.549 --> 00:04:14.992
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

76
00:04:15.292 --> 00:04:18.107
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

